<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Haine is a river in the Belgian province of Hainaut and the French Nord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>. It flows west past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> and through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borinage">Borinage</a> coalfield to join the Scheldt at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conde-sur-lescaut">Condé-sur-l'Escaut</a>. The medieval County of Hainaut, and the modern Belgian province, take their name from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haine.jpg" alt="Haine" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Havr%C3%A9_JPG05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
